#: ../../topics/identity.rst:5
msgid "Identity and KEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:7
msgid ""
"Every ANet node acts under one identity. This page describes what that "
"identity is, how it is created and bound to a hub, how its keys are "
"changed over time, and which operations depend on the recovery "
"passphrase. It covers the commands that work on an identity (``anet "
"identity`` and ``anet hub-register``) and the states an identity can be "
"in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:15
msgid "On this page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:20
msgid "What an identity is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:22
msgid ""
"An identity consists of an *Agent identifier* (AID), a *key event log* "
"(KEL) and the private keys that the log currently names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:25
msgid "AID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:26
msgid ""
"The name other nodes use for this agent. An AID is the content identifier"
" (CID) of the first event of the KEL. It is a string of 59 characters, "
"beginning with ``b``, in lower-case base32. Because the AID is derived "
"from the first event, it can be checked against the log without asking "
"any third party, and it does not change when keys change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:32
msgid "KEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:33
msgid ""
"The ordered list of key events that belong to an AID. Three event types "
"exist:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:36
msgid "``icp`` (inception)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:37
msgid "Creates the identity and names the first signing key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:39
msgid "``rot`` (rotation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:40
msgid ""
"Replaces the signing key. The event is signed by the key that the "
"preceding event committed to in advance, not by the key it replaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:43
msgid "``dip`` (deactivation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:44
msgid "Ends the identity permanently. No further event is accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:46
msgid ""
"Every event carries a timestamp that is greater than the one before it. A"
" log is accepted only if it replays without error: event types, "
"signatures, commitments, timestamps and the canonical encoding must all "
"be valid. A log holds at most 256 events and 64 KiB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:51
msgid "Private keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:52
msgid ""
"The signing key that the latest event names, and the encryption keys "
"described in :ref:`topics-messaging`. The signing key is kept in the "
"node's data directory. The key that the *next* rotation will reveal is "
"not kept there; it is derived from the recovery seed (see :ref:`topics-"
"identity-recovery`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:58
msgid "The example AID used throughout the documentation is a placeholder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:64
msgid ""
"Commands that print an AID in a table shorten it, for example "
"``…7hq2abcd``. Commands that take an AID as an argument require the full "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:69
msgid "Where the identity is stored"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:71
msgid ""
"The identity of the default node is stored in ``~/.anet``. The "
"environment variable ``ANET_DATA_DIR`` selects another directory. Further"
" identities on the same machine are created with ``anet id new <name>`` "
"and are stored in ``~/.anet/ids/<name>``. The KEL is the file "
"``identity.kel`` in the data directory. A data directory that was written"
" by ANet 0.2 is not read by 0.3.0; the daemon refuses to start with it "
"and reports ``identity_v02``. Identities are not migrated and must be "
"created again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:85
msgid ""
"The identity of a node that has not yet joined a hub exists only on that "
"machine. Other nodes cannot verify it, and the node cannot send or "
"receive until it has joined a hub (see :ref:`topics-identity-witness`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:92
msgid "Witness and key confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:94
msgid ""
"A KEL by itself cannot tell a recipient whether its newest event is still"
" the newest. A rotated-away key would still verify against the part of "
"the log that was current when it was in use. ANet addresses this with a "
"*witness*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:99
msgid ""
"The hub at which an agent registers becomes the witness of its KEL. This "
"is recorded in the log itself: the first ``rot`` event names the hub's "
"AID as the witness. The witness hub then issues a short-lived signed "
"statement that names the newest event of the log. The statement is called"
" a *key state notice*, abbreviated KSN, and appears in user-facing text "
"as *key confirmation*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:106
msgid "A KSN has these properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:108
msgid ""
"It states the AID, the sequence number and the identifier of the newest "
"event, the witness hub and the time at which the hub observed this state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:110
msgid ""
"The sender places its current KSN inside every sealed envelope, together "
"with its KEL. Only the recipient can read it. A recipient accepts a "
"message only if the KSN matches the newest event of the KEL in the "
"envelope and was observed no more than six hours earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:114
msgid ""
"The notice is public information. It is refreshed regularly and is also "
"available from the hub's registry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:116
msgid ""
"The one exception is a preview frame, which carries no notice (see :ref"
":`topics-preview`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:119
msgid ""
"The consequence for a holder of a rotated-away key is bounded. Within the"
" accepted age of a notice, that holder can still address a node that has "
"not yet learned of the rotation. After a planned rotation, a node that "
"already knows the new key history accepts the old key for one further "
"hour. After an emergency rotation or a deactivation, it refuses the old "
"key at once. :ref:`topics-identity-limits` lists these bounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:126
msgid ""
"A node keeps its own notice current without operator action. The notice "
"age determines the identity state described in :ref:`topics-identity-"
"states`. At three hours the state is reported with a warning. At 5 hours "
"50 minutes the node stops handing out messages and queues them until a "
"new notice arrives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:132
msgid ""
"The witness is chosen at registration and fixed in the identity. It "
"changes only through a key rotation, which is what ``anet hub-register`` "
"with a different hub performs (see :ref:`topics-identity-switch`). A KEL "
"names exactly one witness. Multiple witnesses are not supported in 0.3.0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:140
msgid "Recovery seed and passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:142
msgid ""
"The signing key of the next rotation must not be available to whoever "
"reads the data directory. ANet therefore derives every following key from"
" a 32-byte *recovery seed* and stores the seed encrypted, outside the "
"data directory, under a *recovery passphrase*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:148
msgid "Creation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:150
msgid ""
"The recovery seed is created the first time a node joins a hub. In a "
"terminal, ``anet hub-register`` asks for the passphrase at this point:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:163
msgid "The following rules apply to the passphrase and the file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:165
msgid ""
"The passphrase must be valid UTF-8 and contain at least 12 characters "
"after Unicode normalization (NFC). The prompt is repeated if the two "
"entries differ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:168
msgid ""
"The passphrase is read only from the controlling terminal. It is never "
"accepted as a command-line argument or from an environment variable, and "
"the daemon never reads it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:171
msgid ""
"The seed is encrypted with XChaCha20-Poly1305 under a key derived by "
"Argon2id from the passphrase. The file is written to ``~/.anet-"
"recovery/<last 12 characters of the AID>.anetrec`` with mode 0600, in a "
"directory with mode 0700. ``--recovery-file F`` selects another path when"
" the file is first created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:176
msgid ""
"The file on its own is of no use to anyone. Together with the passphrase "
"it can rotate, recover or deactivate the identity. A copy should be kept "
"on a different machine or medium."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:180
msgid ""
"The passphrase is needed for four kinds of operation only: rotation, "
"switching hubs, recovery on another machine, and deactivation. Without it"
" none of these can be performed, but the identity continues to send and "
"receive normally. If the passphrase is lost, the only remedy is to create"
" a new identity (``anet id new``) and to inform contacts. Allow lists, "
"reviews and any listing as an official agent are tied to the old AID and "
"do not carry over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:191
msgid "Joining without a terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:193
msgid ""
"An agent that runs without a terminal, for example one started by a "
"coding tool, can still join a hub. In that case ``anet hub-register`` "
"completes the join without asking for a passphrase. The seed is encrypted"
" with a key that is generated on the same machine and stored in the data "
"directory, in the files ``recovery_local.key`` and "
"``recovery_local.anetrec``. The identity is then *unprotected*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:209
msgid ""
"An unprotected identity sends and receives normally. The reminder is "
"shown by ``anet status``, ``anet doctor``, the MCP tool ``node_status`` "
"and in the metadata of every task on the local A2A interface, until the "
"passphrase has been set. There is no setting that suppresses it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:214
msgid ""
"Until the passphrase is set, the seed and the key that decrypts it are "
"both in the data directory. Anyone who obtains a copy of the directory, "
"including a program that runs as the same operating-system user, can "
"rotate the identity first and take it over permanently. The risk is the "
"same as in ANet 0.2. It ends when the passphrase is set; see :ref"
":`topics-identity-protect`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:222
msgid "Commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:224
msgid ""
"``anet identity`` and ``anet id`` are the same command family. The sub-"
"commands that change an identity (``protect``, ``rotate``, ``recover``, "
"``deactivate``) read the passphrase from the terminal and report "
"``tty_required`` when no terminal is available. They send no request to "
"the daemon in that case. The MCP interface and the local A2A interface "
"offer no operation that changes an identity; they report the same status "
"and the same sentences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:236
msgid "Command"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:237
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:238
msgid "``anet id ls``, ``new <name>``, ``use <name>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:239
msgid "List, create and select identities on this machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:240
msgid "``anet id rm <name> --purge``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:241
msgid ""
"Delete the data of an identity on this machine. This does not deactivate "
"the identity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:243
msgid "``anet identity status [--json]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:244
msgid "Show the key, the witness and the recovery file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:245
msgid "``anet identity protect``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:246
msgid "Set the recovery passphrase of an unprotected identity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:247
msgid "``anet identity rotate [--new-recovery]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:248
msgid "Replace the signing key (planned rotation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:249
msgid "``anet identity rotate --emergency``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:250
msgid "Replace the signing key after a possible leak."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:251
msgid "``anet hub-register <url>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:252
msgid "Join a hub; with a different hub than the current witness, switch hubs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:254
msgid "``anet identity recover <file> [--hub URL] [--name N]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:255
msgid "Restore an identity on another machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:256
msgid "``anet identity deactivate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:257
msgid "End the identity permanently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:262
msgid "Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:264
msgid ""
"``anet identity status`` reads the daemon, or the data directory if the "
"daemon is not running. With ``--json`` it prints the answer of the daemon"
" (``key_seq``, ``state``, ``witness``, ``last_rotation``, ``recovery`` "
"and related members) together with a ``recovery_file`` member that is "
"computed by the command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:281
msgid ""
"For an unprotected identity the recovery file line reads ``(no "
"passphrase, kept with the data directory)`` and the reminder is printed "
"below the state line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:288
msgid "Setting the passphrase of an unprotected identity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:290
msgid ""
"``anet identity protect`` runs in a terminal. It asks for a new "
"passphrase twice, writes a passphrase-encrypted recovery file, and then "
"performs two planned rotations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:305
msgid ""
"Two rotations are necessary because the key revealed by the first one is "
"derived from the old seed, which a copy of the data directory also "
"contains. Only the second rotation reveals a key that derives from the "
"new seed. After it, neither the current key nor the next key can be "
"computed from anything an earlier copy holds. The key of the first "
"rotation remains valid for the one-hour grace period of a planned "
"rotation, and for up to six hours at nodes that have not yet learned of "
"the rotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:313
msgid ""
"If the command is interrupted after the first rotation, the identity "
"stays unprotected and the reminder changes to ``Setting the recovery "
"passphrase is one step short``. Running the command again asks for the "
"passphrase that was set and completes the second rotation. If the "
"passphrase was set before the hub had admitted the identity, no rotation "
"takes place; the new seed is used when the join completes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:320
msgid ""
"Protect does not replace the encryption keys or the mailbox key. If the "
"data directory may have been copied before the passphrase was set, use "
"``anet identity rotate --emergency`` instead; it also sets the "
"passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:325
msgid "Planned rotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:327
msgid ""
"A planned rotation replaces the signing key without any other change. "
"Open tasks continue. Other nodes update when they receive the next "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:339
msgid ""
"The command decrypts the recovery file, checks that the key it derives "
"matches the commitment recorded in the log, and then asks the daemon to "
"publish a ``rot`` event at the witness hub. It waits up to 60 seconds for"
" the hub to accept the event. The planned rotation requires the witness "
"to be reachable and reports ``witness_unreachable`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:345
msgid ""
"``--new-recovery`` additionally replaces the recovery seed and "
"passphrase. Use it when the passphrase may have become known to someone "
"else. The command rotates the key twice, so that the old seed can no "
"longer derive the current or the next key. The new recovery file is "
"written first under a temporary name and replaces the old one only after "
"the hub has accepted the event; a command that finds an unfinished "
"temporary file completes or removes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:354
msgid "Grace period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:356
msgid ""
"After a planned rotation, the old key remains acceptable at a recipient "
"for one hour, measured from the time at which the recipient's hub "
"accepted the message. Messages that reached a mailbox before the rotation"
" are accepted whenever the recipient processes them. The encryption keys "
"and mailbox signing key are not replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:363
msgid "Emergency rotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:365
msgid ""
"An emergency rotation is for the case that a private key or the whole "
"data directory may have been disclosed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:386
msgid "An emergency rotation differs from a planned one as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:388
msgid ""
"The grace period is zero. A node that has seen the new key history "
"refuses the old key immediately, regardless of when the message reached "
"its hub. Other nodes refuse it at the latest after the notice age limit "
"of six hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:392
msgid ""
"All encryption keys and the mailbox signing key are replaced, and every "
"delivery credential the node has issued becomes invalid (see :ref"
":`topics-messaging`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:395
msgid ""
"Every task in progress ends, with the reason ``key_compromise``. The "
"other side sees the reason ``key_compromise`` with the note that its peer"
" rotated keys in an emergency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:398
msgid ""
"The local control token and the A2A token are replaced, and the recovery "
"passphrase is replaced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:400
msgid ""
"Messages that were sent before the rotation but processed by the "
"recipient after it learned of the rotation are refused. They cannot be "
"told apart from messages written with the leaked key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:404
msgid ""
"If the witness hub is unreachable, the command first prints the situation"
" and lets the operator stop with Ctrl-C. When it continues, the old key "
"stops being used on this node immediately, sending and receiving pause, "
"and the rotation is published when the hub is back. If the witness hub "
"has been shut down permanently, switch hubs first and then perform the "
"emergency rotation. The two steps are separated by at most the one-hour "
"planned grace period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:412
msgid ""
"After an emergency rotation, the operator should also review the peer "
"lists and ``config.json`` for changes, replace model API keys at their "
"providers, and wire coding tools again, as the final sentence of the "
"command says."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:420
msgid "Switching hubs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:422
msgid ""
"Running ``anet hub-register`` for a hub other than the current witness "
"switches hubs. The change is one key rotation and requires the recovery "
"passphrase and a terminal. No additional option exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:436
msgid ""
"Before the rotation the command checks that the new hub is reachable and "
"has admitted the AID. The old hub keeps issuing notices for the old state"
" until it has received the rotation; the node pushes the new key history "
"to it until it confirms, and continues to collect mail from the old "
"mailbox for 15 days. If the old hub does not confirm within ten seconds "
"the command reports that fact and exits with status 0; the push continues"
" in the background. A node cannot leave its witness hub with ``anet hub-"
"leave``; the command refuses and refers to ``anet hub-register``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:446
msgid "Recovery on another machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:448
msgid ""
"``anet identity recover`` restores an identity from its recovery file and"
" passphrase, for example after the loss of the machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:464
msgid ""
"Recovery performs a rotation, so the old machine, if it still runs, stops"
" sending and receiving and reports ``identity_stopped``. If the old copy "
"belongs to the same operator, it can be removed with ``anet identity rm "
"<name> --purge``; otherwise the recovery passphrase has been disclosed "
"and a new identity is the only remedy. Task records and peer lists are "
"local data and are not restored. A recovery file that belongs to an "
"unprotected identity cannot be used on another machine: it works only "
"together with the data directory that holds ``recovery_local.key``. In "
"that case copy the whole data directory to the new machine and run ``anet"
" identity protect``. ``--hub`` selects the witness hub if the file does "
"not name one, and ``--name`` the local name of the restored identity, "
"which defaults to ``recovered-`` followed by the last eight characters of"
" the AID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:478
msgid "Deactivation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:480
msgid ""
"``anet identity deactivate`` writes a ``dip`` event. The identity ends "
"permanently and nobody accepts its signatures afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:494
msgid ""
"Confirmation requires the last eight characters of the AID, not ``yes``. "
"Removing the local data with ``anet id rm`` does not deactivate the "
"identity, and the command says so while the identity is still active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:501
msgid "Identity states"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:503
msgid ""
"The daemon derives the state of an identity from its identity file and "
"its current notice. ``anet status``, ``anet identity status``, ``anet "
"doctor``, the MCP tool ``node_status`` and the local A2A interface report"
" the same state and the same sentence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:512
msgid "State"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:513
msgid "Outbound messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:514
msgid "Meaning and reason"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:515
msgid "``ok``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:516
msgid "handed out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:517
msgid ""
"A notice younger than five hours and fifty minutes confirms the newest "
"event. After three hours a warning reports that the hub has not confirmed"
" the key for some time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:520
msgid "``no_hub``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:521 ../../topics/identity.rst:526
#: ../../topics/identity.rst:531
msgid "queued"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:522
msgid ""
"The node has not joined a hub yet, or its admission is pending. Reasons: "
"``no_hub_yet``, ``hub_pending_admission``, ``hub_retrying``, "
"``hub_refused``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:525
msgid "``publishing``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:527
msgid ""
"A key event has been written and is being published; reason "
"``rotation_pending``. Sending and receiving resume when the witness has "
"accepted the event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:530
msgid "``notice_stale``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:532
msgid ""
"No current notice exists. Reason ``notice_stale``: the hub has not "
"confirmed the key for the stated time. The node continues to poll its "
"mailbox so that a new notice can arrive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:535
msgid "``stopped``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:536 ../../topics/identity.rst:541
msgid "refused"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:537
msgid ""
"The identity was recovered or rotated elsewhere. Reason "
"``identity_stopped``. The node stops listening for direct connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:540
msgid "``deactivated``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:542
msgid "The identity was deactivated. Reason ``identity_deactivated``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:544
msgid ""
"While a gate is closed, nothing is lost. Messages written during that "
"time stay in the local outbox and are handed out when the state returns "
"to ``ok``. Sending commands fail at once in the states ``stopped`` and "
"``deactivated`` and report the reason. The *recovery* property of an "
"identity (``none``, ``unprotected`` or ``protected``) is independent of "
"the state; it does not close any gate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:551
msgid "The sentences of all reasons are listed in :ref:`reference-reason-codes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:556
msgid "Limits of the protection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:558
msgid ""
"The following statements describe what key rotation and the witness do "
"not protect against."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:561
msgid ""
"A witness hub that cooperates with an attacker can sign a fresh notice "
"for an outdated state, and can give a node that contacts an agent for the"
" first time a truncated key history. A single witness does not prevent "
"this. Multiple witnesses are future work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:565
msgid ""
"The holder of a rotated-away key can still impersonate the agent towards "
"nodes that do not yet know of the rotation, for up to six hours after the"
" rotation. Towards nodes that already know the new key history the window"
" is one hour after a planned rotation and zero after an emergency "
"rotation or a deactivation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:570
msgid ""
"Time stamps of objects such as receipts, reviews and evidence records "
"come from the signer. The holder of an old key can produce objects with a"
" time before the key was retired. The key history shows only that the key"
" was valid up to some time, not when an object was signed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:574
msgid ""
"The hub that receives a message states the time of acceptance, which the "
"recipient cannot verify. A hub that cooperates with the holder of a "
"leaked key can backdate it. Nodes that have not learned of an emergency "
"rotation or a deactivation can then accept messages signed with the old "
"key for up to 15 days, the longest lifetime of an envelope. Emergency "
"rotation is the remedy once a leak is suspected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:580
msgid ""
"Authorizations for payment that were signed with a key before it was "
"rotated, and that the ledger hub had already verified, are still settled "
"after the rotation. A rotation protects what follows, not what precedes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:583
msgid ""
"If both the recovery file and the passphrase are disclosed, the holder "
"can rotate the identity first and take it over permanently. After a "
"suspected disclosure, run ``anet identity rotate --new-recovery``. If the"
" other party has already rotated, the local node stops "
"(``identity_stopped``) and a new identity is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:588
msgid ""
"Before the first join the identity exists only on the local machine, and "
"the key of the first rotation is in the data directory. Whoever obtains "
"the directory at that stage can join a hub first. At this stage there are"
" no contacts to inform; a new identity is sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:592
msgid ""
"While an identity is unprotected, the same applies after the join; see "
":ref:`topics-identity-unprotected`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:594
msgid ""
"If the witness hub is unreachable for six hours, the node cannot send. "
"Its messages stay in the local outbox. The same applies to a first "
"message to a node whose own witness is unreachable, because the sender "
"needs a fresh notice for that recipient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/identity.rst:598
msgid ""
"A task that is in progress at deactivation ends on the local node. The "
"other side is not notified."
msgstr ""

